  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1101 PM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nGlobal models suggest that a weak mid/upper-level low (initially \nacross the central Appalachians) will phase with a smaller \ndisturbance to its east later this week to form a deep low that \nwill sit off the northern Mid-Atlantic Coast this weekend. This \nwill ensure a continuation of dry NNW flow aloft across the TN \nValley for much of the period, before this regime weakens Saturday\nand Sunday. With indications that low-level confluence across \nwill progressively diminish on Thursday/Friday, the risk for \nshowers in the east will continue to fall as light N-NE flow \nadvects a drier airmass into the region from a high across \nsoutheastern Canada. Highs will be in the l-m 80s, with overnight \nlows dropping into the m-u 50s this weekend (when dewpoints could \ndrop into the 40s).",
